162:Let $T\in \mathbb{H}^{n_1}\otimes_{\mathbb{H}}\mathbb{H}^{n_2}\otimes_{\mathbb{H}}\mathbb{H}^{n_3}$ where $2\leq n_i\leq 3$. Then in the $2\times 2\times 2$ case, there exists an explicit decompositon of $T$ into $3$ simple tensors, so $\rank(T)\leq 3$. Furthermore, $\rank(T)\leq 3$ if $n_i=3$ for exactly one $i$, $\rank(T)\leq 4$ if $n_i=2$ for exactly one $i$, and $\rank(T)\leq 6$ in the $3\times 3\times 3$ case.
