+        "They define P exactly by",
+        "  P[row_for_word[x], y] = row_signs[x] * (-1)^popcount(x & y)",
+        "for 0 <= x,y < n. Here '&' is bitwise AND and popcount counts 1-bits.",
+        "This P is invertible and P^{-1}=P^T/n. Order matters in both lists.",
